  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 - SHO Turkiye Earthquake -2 pledges MDRTR004 M2304107 (2023) and MDRTR004 M2404070 (2024)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A magnitude 7.7 earthquake occurred in T&#xfc;rkiye at 4:17 am on 6 February 2023. Eighty-three aftershocks at a magnitude 7.7 earthquake occurred in T&#xfc;rkiye at 4:17 am on 6 February 2023. Eighty-three aftershocks at a maximum level of 6.7 followed the initial earthquake, and an additional separate earthquake of 7.6 occurred at 1:24 pm the following day in the same region.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Across the 10 provinces affected by the earthquake in Kahramanmara&#x15f;, Gaziantep, Hatay, Ad&#x131;yaman, Malatya, Osmaniye, Kilis, Adana, Sanliurfa and Diyarbakir.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this Emergency Appeal (EA), TRC is aiming to expand their support to around 300,000 people in 10 cities who have been severely affected mainly due to the demolition of their houses in the earthquake.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this Emergency Appeal the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC) aims to support the TRC in the response to the Kahramamara&#x15f; Earthquake Operation. The strategy of the IFRC&#x2019;s response will be to meet the immediate and early recovery needs of approximately 300,000 people affected in Kahramanmara&#x15f; province and the surrounding provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
